<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via four-day fixed system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via four-day fixed system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve injected reserves into the banking system on Thursday through four-day fixed system repurchase agreements, a Fed spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The add move was mostly in line with the market's expectations.</p>
<p>At 1030 EST/1530 GMT, the time the Fed usually intervenes in the market, the federal funds rate traded at 5-3/16 percent, below the Fed's 5-1/4 percent target.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1676 ))</p>
</text>
